tasks.condition:
Tell your friends a few words about:
a) your last summer trip;
b) your last winter trip;
c) your trip to the seaside;
d) your trip by plane;
e) your trip by train.

Imagine you are Ann. Tell the class about:
a) your journey to Odessa;
b) your stay in Odessa;
c) your voyage on board the ship.

Imagine that you are Laura Smith (see Exercise 4). You have to buy a ticket to Leeds. Go to the railway station
a) Say how to get there from your house (Exercise 4 can help you);
b) Role-play the dialogue at the railway station when you buy a ticket (Exercise 13, Lesson 33 can help you).

Tell your classmates:
1. what a hobby is;
2. what hobbies you know;
3. what things people usually collect;
4. what a thematic collection is;
5. what your favourite hobby is.

Look at the pictures and say:
1. what you usually do at this time;
2. what you did yesterday.

Say what the members of your family:
a) usually do:
b) did yesterday at this time;
c) decided to do on Sunday.
1) at a quarter to seven;
2) at half past three;
3) at ten to four;
4) at quarter past nine;
5) at twenty to ten.

Work in pairs and ask each other:
a) what is on at some cinemas and theatres of your city (town);
b) what is on at your local cinema house. Describe the film which is on.

Tell your classmates about:
1. your favourite Disney cartoon;
2. your favourite Russian cartoon.

Which of your family is a theatregoer? Do you know:
a) which is his / her favourite theatre;
b) what he / she likes best (operas, ballets, plays, other performances)?

Look at the pictures and say what George has done:
1) for 35 years;
2) since his ship went under the sea.

Look at the words and say what the girls have done together.
Example: The girls have prepared for the meeting together.
to prepare for the meeting;
to prepare coffee;
to prepare turkey;
to prepare dinner;
to prepare for a harvest festival.

Tell your classmates about:
a) the discovery of America;
b) the first English settlements in the New World.

You  want to do the following:
1. to prepare turkey for Xmas;
2. To take your father’s gun and go hunting;
3. To sell a gold coin from your granny’s collection;
4. To sail to America;
5. To  sell all the harvest from your garden;
6. To buy a snake.
Ask you mother’s permission and write your questions and possible answers.

tasks.solution:
a) between spring and autumn — summer,
autumn and spring — winter;
b) between February and April — March;
May and July — June;
September and November — October;
December and February — January.
c) between Tuesday and Thursday — Wednesday;
Friday and Sunday — Saturday.
Перевод:
а) между весной и осенью — лето,
осенью и весной — зима;
b) между февралем и апрелем — март;
маем и июлем — июнь;
сентябрем и ноябрем — октябрь;
декабрем и февралем — январь.
c) между вторником и четвергом — среда;
пятницей и воскресеньем — суббота.

tasks.condition:
You have come to a small town in Canada. Your host and hostess have never been to Russia. They ask you to tell about:
1. Moscow;
2. St. Petersburg;
3. The war of 1812;
4. the Russian people and their country.
What will you tell them?
